Pear desktop test package
===========================

Target: Debian/Ubuntu-based systems with an Xfce X11 desktop. Linux Mint Xfce
is the primary development environment. Other distributions are unverified.
The architecture-independent package contains Python source and image assets.

Download the .deb attachment from a published release:

    https://github.com/orha9n/pear-desktop/releases

Open a terminal in the folder containing the downloaded .deb. Check its filename
with ls. A GitHub source ZIP or tarball is not an installable package.

Install with apt so dependencies are resolved (run apt update first to avoid
404 errors from superseded Ubuntu security packages):

    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install ./pear-desktop_0.1.0.alpha1_all.deb

Log into Xfce using X11, then run as your regular desktop user:

    pear-setup

Alternatively, open "Pear Setup" from the applications menu. Initial setup
requires internet to fetch pinned external themes, and may request sudo for
the system GTK theme and wallpaper. Log out and in after setup for global menus.
Installing the package itself does not change any user's desktop or start Pear.

Check operation with:

    pear status

Restore your original desktop before uninstalling, inside the graphical session:

    pear-reset
    sudo apt remove pear-desktop

Do not run pear-setup or pear-reset with sudo. Package removal does not
automatically restore home-directory settings. Recovery state stays in
~/.local/share/liquid/backups and ~/.config/liquid.

Test on a disposable VM first. This alpha package has automated packaging and
regression checks; a clean-machine graphical install is still required.

Building from a source checkout (not from the installed application directory):

    python3 tools/build_deb.py

Set --maintainer 'Your Name <your-public-email>' for a public release. The local
test build uses an explicit example.invalid address, not a support contact.
